---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
const groups = [
  { t: 'Fit with your frameworks', items: ['Ships with or can hold the control sets you need (ISO 27001, 22301, 9001, national frameworks)', 'Maps one control to several frameworks', 'Lets you add your own policies, obligations and custom frameworks'] },
  { t: 'Data and security', items: ['Hosting location and data residency options that meet your sector rules', 'Role-based access and a full audit trail', 'Support for single sign-on with your identity provider'] },
  { t: 'Day-to-day use', items: ['Occasional users (risk owners, auditees) can complete tasks without training', 'Reminders and escalations for overdue actions', 'Arabic and English support where your users need it'] },
  { t: 'Integration and reporting', items: ['An API to connect HR, ticketing and identity systems', 'Dashboards by entity, department and framework', 'Board and regulator reports generated from live data'] },
  { t: 'Rollout and support', items: ['A phased rollout plan starting with one or two modules', 'Data migration from spreadsheets and existing tools', 'Local support hours that match the Gulf working week'] },
];
---
<Base title="GRC Software Buyer’s Checklist" description="What to check before choosing GRC software in the UAE or Saudi Arabia: framework coverage, data residency, usability, integration and rollout." ogType="article" crumbs={[{ name: 'Resources', href: '/resources/' }, { name: 'GRC software buyer’s checklist' }]}>
  <PageHeader narrow eyebrow="Guide" title="GRC software buyer’s checklist" />
  <article class="container-x max-w-3xl py-12">
    <div class="prose-x">
      <p>Most GRC software demos look alike. The differences show up after go-live: whether risk owners actually log in, whether one control really covers several frameworks, and whether the data can stay where your regulator expects it. Use this list to compare platforms on what matters in the Gulf.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
      {groups.map((g) => (
        <div class="card">
          <p class="font-semibold">{g.t}</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2">{g.items.map((i) => <li class="flex gap-2 text-ink-soft"><span class="text-teal">☐</span>{i}</li>)}</ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="prose-x mt-10">
      <h2>Start smaller than you think</h2>
      <p>The rollouts that stick start with the area causing the most pain, often audit follow-up, the risk register or document control, and add modules once people use the first one every week.</p>
      <h2>Fix the framework first</h2>
      <p>Software automates a process; it doesn’t decide your risk appetite or who owns a control. If those answers aren’t clear yet, a short consulting phase first will save rework.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
  <CtaBand title="Evaluate platforms against this checklist" text="We can turn it into scripted demo scenarios and a scoring sheet, so every vendor is compared on the same terms." href="/enquire/?route=compliance-software" label="Get help choosing" />
</Base>
